      "text": "Did you know?",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Did you know?",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2910,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 252,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 253,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Investment in wind in the US grew from $700 million in 2004 to $18 billion in 2008 ($48 billion worldwide)",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Investment in wind in the US grew from $700 million in 2004 to $18 billion in 2008 ($48 billion worldwide)",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2936,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 254,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 255,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  The US is the world leader in new installations (8,358 MW), total MW (25,000+) and annual output",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  The US is the world leader in new installations (8,358 MW), total MW (25,000+) and annual output",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2962,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 256,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 257,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Wind was 42% of power capacity (MW) added in the US in 2008 — more than any other form of power generation",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Wind was 42% of power capacity (MW) added in the US in 2008 — more than any other form of power generation",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 2988,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 258,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 259,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  In 2008, 35,000 jobs were added in the wind industry, raising the total to more than 85,000",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  In 2008, 35,000 jobs were added in the wind industry, raising the total to more than 85,000",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3014,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 260,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 261,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Over 70 new manufacturing plants or expansions were announced or built since January 2007 in 21 states",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Over 70 new manufacturing plants or expansions were announced or built since January 2007 in 21 states",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3040,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 262,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 263,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  A 2008 DOE study showed it is technically feasible to produce 20% of electricity through wind power by 2030",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  A 2008 DOE study showed it is technically feasible to produce 20% of electricity through wind power by 2030",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3066,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 264,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 265,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Cumulatively, the 20% wind scenario would avoid the consumption of 4 trillion gallons of water through 2030",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Cumulatively, the 20% wind scenario would avoid the consumption of 4 trillion gallons of water through 2030",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3092,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 266,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Each wind turbine provides farm or ranch income annually — $2,000–4,000 per megawatt",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Each wind turbine provides farm or ranch income annually — $2,000–4,000 per megawatt",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3118,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 268,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 269,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Each megawatt (MW) of wind energy capacity installed in the U.S. provides 2.5–3 job-years of employment",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Each megawatt (MW) of wind energy capacity installed in the U.S. provides 2.5–3 job-years of employment",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3144,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 270,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 271,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  To generate the same electricity as a 1-MW wind turbine, a fossil fuel plant requires ~60 million gallons of water/year",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  To generate the same electricity as a 1-MW wind turbine, a fossil fuel plant requires ~60 million gallons of water/year",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li10",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3170,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 272,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 273,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  Wind energy could provide 6% of our nation's electricity by 2020 and 20% by 2030",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  Wind energy could provide 6% of our nation's electricity by 2020 and 20% by 2030",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
    {
      "id": "facts_li11",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80,
      "y": 3196,
      "width": 1280,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 274,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 275,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1708800000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "›  As many as 215,000 new jobs would be created by adding 50,000 MW of new wind installations in the U.S.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "›  As many as 215,000 new jobs would be created by adding 50,000 MW of new wind installations in the U.S.",
      "lineHeight": 1.4
    },
